# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRU PEPTIDE frontend — environment configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is a presentation-only frontend. It runs in one of two modes, selected
# entirely by whether NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is set:
#
#   • UNSET (default) → "reference mode"
#       Catalog reads, pricing computation, and admin mutations run in-browser
#       against bundled reference data. Cart, age verification, and
#       personalization (favorites, saved, recently-viewed, COA downloads) are
#       device-local UI state persisted to localStorage and work with no backend.
#
#       Session/profile and order history/placement have NO reference data:
#       signing in, saving a profile, and placing an order require a backend, so
#       the account dashboard shows a sign-in prompt and checkout reports that it
#       isn't connected yet. Nothing is faked or fabricated.
#
#   • SET → "http mode"
#       All backend boundaries (lib/data/http/*, lib/client/*) issue fetch()
#       calls to your backend at this base URL instead. Implement the REST
#       contract documented in:
#         - lib/data/http/*             (catalog + pricing reads)
#         - lib/client/account.ts       (session/profile + orders)
#         - lib/client/pricing-admin.ts (admin pricing)
#         - lib/client/catalog-admin.ts (admin catalog)
#
# Example: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
